# Central admin vs tenant writer auth

Two separate account types. They must never authenticate against each other's tables.

| | Central admin | Tenant writer |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Guard / provider | `web` / `users` | `writer` / `writers` |
| Model / DB | `App\Models\User`, central DB | `App\Models\Writer`, tenant DB `users` |
| Login | `{centralDomain}/login` | `{tenant-domain}/login` (`writer.login`) |
| Protection | `auth`, `verified`, `admin`, then `can:` per route | `auth:writer` |

## Central roles

- Central users have a nullable `role` (`App\Enums\CentralRole`): `super_admin` or `support`.
  `null` means an ordinary central account with no admin access. The old `is_admin` column is gone;
  never reintroduce it.
- Abilities live in one place, `App\Support\CentralAbility` (Gates registered in `AppServiceProvider`):
  - `super_admin`: every ability.
  - `support`: `ACCESS_ADMIN`, `VIEW_TENANTS`, `VIEW_TENANT_USERS`, `IMPERSONATE_TENANT_USERS` only.
    Support must never create, edit, suspend, reactivate or delete tenants or tenant users.
- Every new admin route sits in the `auth`, `verified`, `admin` group and adds a `can:` middleware
  for the narrowest ability. Form requests check the same ability in `authorize()`.
  Hiding a button in React is not authorization.
- Add new abilities to `CentralAbility::roles()` and `CentralAbility::for()` (shared to React as `auth.can`).

## Rules

- Do not point both providers at the same model, and do not add central roles to tenant users.
- `role` is not fillable. Grant it only via `php artisan admin:promote {email} {--role=} {--force}`
  (`app/Console/Commands/PromoteAdministrator.php`). Keep its safeguard: it refuses when another user
  already has a central role unless `--force` is passed.
- Public registration and profile updates must never set a central role.
- `UseWriterGuard` calls `Auth::shouldUse('writer')` after tenancy is initialized.
  Writer login uses `Auth::guard('writer')` in `App\Http\Requests\Writer\LoginRequest`.
- `TenancyServiceProvider` captures the central guard at boot and restores it on `terminating`.
  Do not read `config('auth.defaults.guard')` inside that callback (it is `writer` by then).
- `bootstrap/app.php` redirects guests/users to `writer.*` routes when tenancy is initialized,
  otherwise to central routes.

## Authorization and mass assignment

- Post ownership is enforced by `PostPolicy` (update/delete only when `user_id` matches).
  Always call `$this->authorize(...)` in writer controllers.
- `Post::$fillable` excludes `user_id` and `cover_image`. Set them server-side:

```php
$post = new Post($this->attributes($request));
$post->user_id = $request->user('writer')->id; // ✅ never from request input
$post->cover_image = TenantCoverImage::sync($request, null);
```
